```
Reason:
The `poll()` function calls `sock_poll_wait()` unconditionally, which causes the function to sleep even when the `need_wakeup` flag is set. This prevents the driver from processing Rx and Tx operations promptly, leading to delays in handling packets until the timeout expires.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (pool->cached_need_wakeup) {
    if (xs->zc)
        xsk_wakeup(xs, pool->cached_need_wakeup);
    else
        __xsk_sendmsg(sk);
} else {
    sock_poll_wait(file, sock, wait);
}
```
Reason:
The patch checks the `cached_need_wakeup` flag before deciding whether to sleep. If the flag is set, it wakes up the driver immediately, ensuring that Rx and Tx processing occurs promptly. Only if the flag is not set does it call `sock_poll_wait()`, allowing the function to sleep only when appropriate.

